                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Liver cirrhosis is a major cause of death worldwide and is characterized by extensive fibrosis. There are currently no effective antifibrotic therapies available. To obtain a better understanding of the cellular and molecular mechanisms involved in disease pathogenesis we profile the transcriptomes of more than 100,000 single human cells from healthy and cirrhotic human liver.",
